      "rows": [
        {
          "qty": "42",
          "label": "Kullervo's Bane",
          "note": "4-6 a run",
          "alt": null,
          "done": false
        },
        {
          "qty": "200",
          "label": "Ueymag",
          "note": "densest inside the Hold",
          "alt": null,
          "done": false
        },
        {
          "qty": "10",
          "label": "Pathos Clamp",
          "note": "10 a kill, 15 on Steel Path",
          "alt": "or 1 per Undercroft side portal",
          "done": true
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        "Bane pays out only if the Kullervo boss and the Orowyrm both die in the same run; killing Kullervo and leaving gives nothing",
        "Kullervo's Hold does not exist during Joy or Envy, so two of the five 2-hour mood windows are dead time",
        "Steel Path pays 6-8 Bane a run instead of 4-6, but the longer run costs more than the extra Bane is worth",
        "Run The Duviri Experience, not The Lone Story; the Hold is a side objective only in the Experience",
        "If The Warden is not above the arena the fight is scheduled as a later main objective, so do not wait for him",
        "Pathos Clamps are immune to Resource Boosters"
      ],
      "bonuses": [
        "Ueymag for both the Chassis and the Systems comes off these same runs",
        "Resources are kept once you earn a Decree, so an abandoned run still keeps the pickups",
        "The Orowyrm that ends every Bane run drops all 10 Pathos Clamps in one kill"
      ],
      "disclosures": [
        {
          "title": "how to beat Kullervo",
          "body": "Three sequential health bars, fought as the Drifter. Primaries do half damage and secondaries two thirds, but finishers do 1.1x, so melee and finishers are the way through. Phase 1 is Collective Curse and the Storm of Ukko knife rain, which a precise Sirocco shot interrupts; phase 2 spawns five blade-throwing copies; phase 3 spawns Persecutor Liminus, and killing them all turns them on Kullervo before his aerial laser barrages, best dodged from a Kaithe. Bring at least 5 Decrees before speaking to The Warden, and Transference Sync to a modded Warframe if it goes badly."
        },
        {
          "title": "why public squads go wrong",
          "body": "Squads farm decrees for 40+ minutes before touching an objective, refuse the Undercroft, and stall on Orowyrm mechanics; one reported run hit 50 minutes and collapsed. Solo, Alchemy and Void Flood take 2-3 minutes each, while the same Alchemy bar crawls with 3-4 players."
        },
        {
          "title": "climbing the Orowyrm",
          "body": "It has no traversal animation, so climbing looks broken: jump off and re-grapple repeatedly to move up the segments. The telegraphed energy ring on a ~30 second cycle knocks you off, so hop off and re-grapple through it. Wyrmlings do not need a Kaithe; step outside the ring of fire or wall-latch and shoot them."
        }
      ]
    },
